\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Room layout, sensor placements, and collection hardware. The co-located FMCW radar and CSI receiver were mounted on wall~4 and wall~2 for training sessions, on wall~3 for validation sessions, and on wall~1 for test sessions; the CSI sender remained fixed on wall~1, so the test placement puts the receiver on the sender's own wall. Photographs show the DreamHAT+ mm-wave radar HAT mounted on its Raspberry Pi host (left) and the ESP32 board used for CSI collection (right).}}{2}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:layout}{{2}{2}{Room layout, sensor placements, and collection hardware. The co-located FMCW radar and CSI receiver were mounted on wall~4 and wall~2 for training sessions, on wall~3 for validation sessions, and on wall~1 for test sessions; the CSI sender remained fixed on wall~1, so the test placement puts the receiver on the sender's own wall. Photographs show the DreamHAT+ mm-wave radar HAT mounted on its Raspberry Pi host (left) and the ESP32 board used for CSI collection (right)}{figure.2}{}}
